    "notes": "After the victory at Salamis in 306 BCE, Antigonus I and his son Demetrius assumed the royal diadem. Antigonus remained king of his vast successor realm until his defeat and death at Ipsus in 301 BCE. ATLAS keeps this Antigonid successor kingdom distinct from the later Antigonid kingship of Macedon represented by Antigonus II."
